  "findings": [
    {
      "area": "Actual generalJ and Gamma/Poisson suppliers",
      "source": "Part3ActualExceptionalJSmallKernel.lean:69-217",
      "finding": "The production principal-power alternating Gamma-series J and exact symmetric Poisson formula are used. Reciprocal Gamma and its native derivative are bounded on the fixed real compact band inside Re(nu)>-1/4. An integrable order-3/8 Poisson weight and the existing logarithmic derivative envelope provide fixed masses, without requested estimate fields."
    },
    {
      "area": "Order-sensitive derivative bound",
      "source": "Part3ActualExceptionalJSmallKernel.lean:130-217",
      "finding": "One D>0 precedes a,nu,q. For0<=a<=7/32,abs(nu)<=a and0<q<=1, the actual native derivative is bounded by D*(1+abs(logq))*q^(-a). Only the factor2^(7/32) uses the fixed cap; the q exponent retains the shrinking radius a."
    },
    {
      "area": "Uniform numerator cancellation including zero",
      "source": "Part3ActualExceptionalJSmallKernel.lean:219-362",
      "finding": "Real mean-value norm control on[-alpha,alpha] gives numerator<=2*alpha*D*(1+abs(logq))*q^(-alpha). sin(pi*alpha/2)>=alpha cancels alpha before division. At zero the actual removable value2*d_orderJ0 is used and bounded by the same pi*D constant. smallKernelConstant is selected from a proved existence theorem, not assumed."
    },
    {
      "area": "Exact positive normalization",
      "source": "Part3ActualExceptionalJSmallKernel.lean:243-287; production Part3ActualJCriticalOrderZero.lean:114-184",
      "finding": "H_alpha=pi*(J_alpha-J_-alpha)/(2*sin(pi*alpha/2)); H_0=2*d_orderJ0. The identity with-(pi/2)*criticalJRealKernel and literal Pascadi(3.18) at r=i*alpha/2 retains pi,2,i and sign. The existing critical quotient/kernel evenness accounts for the paper opposite imaginary representative. No normalized automorphic expansion is asserted."
    },
    {
      "area": "Physical equality and all-mode Fourier HasSum",
      "source": "Part3ActualExceptionalJPacketAdapter.lean:33-216",
      "finding": "Only PacketData.kernel changes to an extension agreeing with H_alpha(q)/q on the physical region. Actual mixed derivative supplies positive-q continuity at alpha=0. Physical/mode equality, integrability and factorization yield the exact HasSum with actualCoeff and completedPacketSum for every positiveY. All source rows/n carriers/signs/modulations/common interval/physical phase survive."
    },
    {
      "area": "Quantitative small-scale restriction",
      "source": "Part3ActualExceptionalJSmallPacketBudget.lean:62-177,270-349",
      "finding": "Every quantitative transform, mode, squared-weight and smoothing result retains Y<=1/16. This places the full support[Y/16,16Y] in(0,1]. Exact measure and reciprocal q give255; endpoint conversion pays16^theta; the small-domain denominator restoration gives G_J=510*B*16^theta*(1+abs(log(Y/16)))/(1+Y). No large-Y decay is inferred."
    },
    {
      "area": "Physical4*pi and A/J scalar geometry",
      "source": "Part3ActualExceptionalJSmallPacketBudget.lean:182-261",
      "finding": "Uses unchanged physicalScalePacket and L=U/nu, with Y=4*pi*sqrt(A*V*U)/(C*sqrt(Z)). The small gate is exactly4096*pi^2*A*V*U<=C^2*Z. Squared threshold comparison retains full16*pi^2 and explicit lambda>=975/4096. It is a normalized positive-transform scalar estimate, not an actual A/J norm or Kim-Sarnak instance."
    },
    {
      "area": "Finite smoothing and unchanged coefficient energy",
      "source": "Part3ActualExceptionalJSmallPacketBudget.lean:263-349",
      "finding": "Uses the exact J finiteCompletedEnergy=sum norm(actualCoeff)*norm(completedPacketSum)^2. Weighted Cauchy pays one actualW factor; the original cutoff supplies rho<=x^eta and the actual derivative/Fourier theorem pays B0*x^(12eta), with B0 chosen before every packet/scale/order/mode set. Energy remains explicit and the small physical gate remains in the final theorem."
    }
  ],
